  "body": "The social foundation's native stack cannot currently merge without a shared-history rebase. This main-target repair preserves every source commit and contributor through normal merge ancestry, so the same inactive implementation can receive full main-branch validation and independent review. It does not change stack metadata or bypass repository protections.\n\n## Scope\n\nIntegrates #356, #360, #365, #366, #367, #377, #382 and #386, on top of the already merged audit #355. The result contains consent-owned relationships, bounded Following/Discover reads, a gated account-only client/API preview, full-schema rehearsal, current-session transaction guards and persistent legacy DM write restrictions. Source branch heads are recorded below.\n\nAll runtime/client activation gates and production migration registration remain as in the reviewed source. This PR is an inactive foundation integration; delegated identities, full account lifecycle, worker/media/notification privacy, mobile flows, rollout qualification and remaining social acceptance gates are not claimed complete. Later #390, #391 and #394 remain separate work and are not superseded here. No manual deployment or production activation was performed.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe integration tree is byte-identical to reconciled #386 except for the already merged webhook-example redaction from main. Normal ancestry contains all eight recorded source heads and current main; diff whitespace validation passed. Locally verified source evidence: #377 complete PostgreSQL schema/migrations and preserved-write pause; #382 82 session HTTP examples with zero failures, 7,464-state session model plus three expected unsafe controls, 21 CI workflow/scope tests; #386 DM write/lifecycle/consent and both real block/send races, complete schema/reapply/pause, positive DM model plus two expected unsafe controls. Strict catalog JSON and CSV passed without weakening the policy. Exact source CI evidence is tracked in the linked PRs; new checks for this integration SHA are required separately.\n\nThis PR starts as draft pending its own exact-head CI and final review. Original PRs and branches stay intact until this replacement is independently approved, merged and verified. No original PR or issue is closed by its creation.\n\n## Preserved source heads\n\n- #356: `c671a5acbe1403ba89d1d70db165b2b327b6cdec`\n- #360: `f52b1f8b906d5bf61774dfaf6b6173233b0d2172`\n- #365: `24590a40787d81a1681cd14a46f2f0ab7cac5632`\n- #366: `6a6d9e02c22eee213cf56787d9de9e4252721fed`\n- #367: `0bac512baed505f7f035f44c022fc0b64405b9e7`\n- #377: `3606fb5c2215e00b1f3661abdf9e969231ac3b36`\n- #382: `2be39150f626dcd5181951532a8ebe25a3ce3fa4`\n- #386: `e03ce193c2e9c6788fad5f1360aef1088006616f`\n\nMain: `7eafd3f479817f267ba0de6592c3e16ea920f4ae`; integration: `af557c19b29a83965ff0d7d11015b7fc15155524`.\n\n\n## Pinned mobile contract boundary\n\nThe existing tdf-app/main gitlink is `790e03e1fb19083a92c2828a8b77ba1016fd53e4`. This PR advances it by one generated-contract-only commit to `c1832c5eb150299c12b36ba156ff38c981a6b046`; the existing pin is its ancestor and the only file changed between these pins is `src/api/generated/types.ts`. No mobile runtime change is introduced relative to the current tdf-app pin. The exact pinned mobile lint/typecheck and test suite are validated by this root PR's CI.\n\nCompanion [tdf-mobile #80](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-mobile/pull/80) remains open. Its mobile-main integration has six conflicts across authentication tests/UI, user profile, Podfile.lock and generated outputs against mobile main `d4a1b17c733f57f912d36e7e396f6869cfd18c8a`. That broader onboarding/RSVP integration is preserved as separate work. This root PR neither changes mobile main nor drops any code from the mobile revision already pinned by tdf-app/main. No mobile PR or branch is closed or deleted.\n\n\nCurrent-main reconciliation: `5fcd17c926a70073c8ef3eda33904e1b207859ee` normally incorporates main `d4bd497df6979f639dcd112e4f60b57f3526b9e0` (concurrent #405 requester names and #404 migration introduction metadata). The mobile gitlink merges both generated-only contract histories, with companion https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/86. All original social source heads remain ancestors. New-head hosted checks and renewed approval are required. Local validation: focused social/access-request UI, release/CI assertions and strict catalog pass; mobile lint/typecheck pass; full mobile run had 326 passes and one five-second timeout, while the unchanged TicketCheckout suite passed independently. No timeout or assertion was weakened.",
